post_install() {
	cat <<EOF

spnav-onshape-bridge installed. A few steps can't be automated by pacman -
see /usr/share/doc/spnav-onshape-bridge/README.md for the full walkthrough,
or run the guided checklist:

    spnav-onshape-bridge --doctor

Short version:
  1. Make sure spacenavd is running (systemctl status spacenavd).
     If it isn't installed, spacenavd itself is AUR-only.
  2. Run spnav-onshape-bridge once to generate its certificate, then:
     /usr/share/spnav-onshape-bridge/nss-trust-install.sh
  3. Load the browser extension (Chromium) or userscript (Firefox) from
     /usr/share/spnav-onshape-bridge/browser-extension/
  4. Enable the per-user service:
     systemctl --user enable --now spnav-onshape-bridge
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
	post_install
}
